# Vuka Content & IA Rules

All copy lives in `docs/vuka-website-copy-complete.md`. Import via `src/data/` — do not paraphrase.

## Voice

- Direct, declarative, minimal — one strong sentence beats three qualifying ones
- Brand name: lowercase **vuka** in body copy
- Sentence case headings; ALL CAPS only for eyebrows via `Eyebrow` component
- "You" ≥ 1.5× "we" on every page
- Em-dashes over parentheses. Oxford comma. No exclamation marks. No emoji.

## Banned words

passionate, disruptive, ecosystem play, value-add, synergies, scalable solutions, world-class, transformative, revolutionary, next-generation, empower, leverage, facilitate, cohort, demo day, curriculum, pitch coaching, graduate

## Audience routing CTAs

Name the action, not the mechanism:
- ✅ `Start a spinout conversation` — ❌ `Contact us`
- ✅ `Apply to Founder-in-Residence` — ❌ `Learn more`

Primary site CTA everywhere: **work with us** → `/work-with-us`

## Content scope by page

| Argument | Allowed on |
|----------|------------|
| Venture Engines thesis | All pages |
| $100 Problem / access gap | `/founders`, `/partners`, `/our-thesis` only |
| Stage honesty | `/investors` (explicit), elsewhere (implicit) |
| "Startup speed" | Government pages — always define: "a working service in 90 days, not an 18-month implementation plan" |

## Geography

Name cities: Dar es Salaam, Nairobi, Kampala. Not "Africa" alone when EA-specific.

## Routes (launch)

```
/  /what-we-do  /what-we-do/{4-pathways}
/who-we-work-with  /{founders|corporates|government|investors|partners}
/our-thesis  /our-thesis/[slug]
/studio-journal  /studio-journal/[slug]
/work-with-us
```

Portfolio: **omit from nav and sitemap at launch**. MDX in `src/content/portfolio/` — not Medium.

## Portfolio assets & schema

Drop logo files in `public/assets/portfolio/`:

```
public/assets/portfolio/
  ventures/
    hakiki.svg          # venture logo (prefer SVG)
    hakiki-dark.svg     # optional — for dark/emer sections
  clients/
    hakiki/
      tosci.svg
      asa.svg
      ttcl.svg
      aatf.svg
```

Naming: lowercase, hyphenated (`client-name.svg`). SVG preferred; PNG only if no vector available (min 2× retina).

**MDX frontmatter:**

```yaml
logo: /assets/portfolio/ventures/hakiki.svg
logoDark: /assets/portfolio/ventures/hakiki-dark.svg  # optional
clientLogos:
  - name: TOSCI
    src: /assets/portfolio/clients/hakiki/tosci.svg
published: false   # flip true when venture is public-ready
```

URL slug is the filename (`hakiki.mdx` → `/portfolio/hakiki`).

`clientLogos` renders on the case study page only — not on the index card grid (keeps cards clean). Venture logo appears on both grid card and case study hero.

## Medium → site mapping

When syncing Medium posts:
- Title, date, author, reading time → frontmatter
- First paragraph → card excerpt
- Medium tags → site filter tags: `Studio model`, `Infrastructure`, `AI & tools`, `East Africa`, `Founder stories`, `Government & public sector`
- Canonical URL → original Medium post (SEO)
- Publication tag `thesis` vs `journal` → route prefix

## Form (`/work-with-us`)

Fields: name, organisation (optional), enquiry type (6 options + "something else"), message.
Success copy redirects visitor to `/our-thesis`. Email: `hello@vukaventures.co`.

## SEO per page

- Title: `{Page} · vuka.` — homepage: `vuka. · East Africa's venture studio`
- Description: first sentence of page sub-copy
- OG image: typography-led, parchment bg, no stock photos
